<<~ ahu slot=`#/placement-step-2-source-and-record-measurement`>>

! Placement step 2 — source and record measurement

Expanded the read-only inventory in `PLACE-MEASURE.md`. It now distinguishes persisted and in-memory families, names their current stores and readers, lists family-level test coverage, and records that INGEST's `source` and `to` remain independent. `vessel-island-pool-core.ts:resolveDiskMirrors` intersects recipe designation with the vessel's mirror grant and sends concrete per-wiki mirror entries in the manifest, but `IslandContext` and ACTION handlers do not currently receive that registry.

Key placement findings: outcomes and receipt facts currently use the daemon wiki working slot; daemon document holds mailbox and lease epochs; ward audits use default writable; residency effects remain in each affected bag and have a distinct record shape; secrets and dyads currently share the daemon document; persona acts live in persona plane with an admission duplicate in daemon; signed swarm acts live on a promote board while transient swarm controls live in the daemon wiki. Delegate and face-row request rows are in-memory/socket flows, not stored records. Realm announcements live in the crossroads document. `cap/**` lives in the daemon document through its composite.

The measurement does not grant authority to move a record family: Step 3 must introduce explicit homes and thread those handles to all identified writers/readers. No records moved in this step.

`PLACE-RULING.md` is not needed yet; target home names and placement follows the operator's explicit ruling. The sources do not settle whether lower-level signed swarm board records should move with `swarm controls`; the operator names the controls and the existing architecture assigns the signed acts to a different face promote board. Keep that distinct unless a concrete writer/read contract proves otherwise.

Suggested commit subject: `lar:///placement.measures/record-homes`

<<~/ahu>>

